# OVERLAY "fast_acc" — the speed variant PLUS the acceleration it needs to
# actually reach that speed. Applied after holybro_sitl.parm.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS, and it was measured rather than guessed. Flying `fast.parm`
# (WP_SPD 1.0, WP_ACC left at 0.6) over seed 1 on 2026-09-15 moved the p90
# ground speed from 0.19 to 0.32 m/s but the PEAK went DOWN, 0.43 to 0.36. The
# ceiling was never reached: at 0.6 m/s/s, getting to 1.0 m/s takes 1.67 s and
# 0.83 m, and stopping takes the same again, so no leg shorter than ~1.7 m ever
# cruises at all. Raising the speed limit alone is half a change.
#
# THE RISK THIS TAKES, stated plainly, because it is the one the base file
# warns about: acceleration is what the airframe FEELS when a new setpoint
# appears, and BiguaSim's 0.3-0.5 s actuation lag turns a sharp demand into an
# oscillation (~/work/biguasim-problems.md, 2026-08-18). 1.0 is a modest step
# from 0.6 and still well under the 2.5 default — but if this config oscillates,
# the seed sweep sees it as fewer valid landings and more VO drift, which is
# exactly why it is a separate row in the table instead of folded into `fast`.
WP_SPD          1.0
WP_ACC          1.0
ATC_RATE_WPY_MAX 25
